1
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,637
Sir, Aka says he spotted a monster
ahead that looks like the King of Souls.

2
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:14,779
We found him, huh?

3
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,837
Everyone's depending on us, Boxxo.

4
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:18,979
Let's do our best!

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,590
Hello there!

6
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,260
How's it looking?

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,617
The King of Souls and some monsters
under his command are just ahead.

8
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,320
There are five corpse fiends, five undead,

9
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:39,440
eight skeleton fiends,
and four flame skulls.

10
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,740
There are 22 bodyguards in total.

11
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:44,058
Not impossible, but not easy either.

12
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,177
If the Vice Captain were here, we could
just wipe them all out with magic.

13
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:52,077
I mean, I could probably take down a
couple of them before they got too close.

14
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,101
We should whittle down their numbers
before we engage them head on.

15
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:58,317
Mr. Boxo?

16
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,106
Have you come up with a plan?

17
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,257
It looks like the device
that sprays out water.

18
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:12,037
I bet something probably comes out
of the tip if you pull the trigger.

19
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:12,950
Hello there!

20
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,940
Whoa, you were right!

21
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:16,940
Ugh, stuff stinks!

22
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:21,660
Is this mystery liquid
safe to touch? Hello there!

23
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:26,757
It feels greasy and it
kind of reminds me of oil.

24
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,520
I wonder if it'll burn.

25
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,640
It's incredibly volatile.

26
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:36,197
Are you suggesting we douse the
enemy in this flammable oil?

27
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,110
Hello there.

28
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,600
Okay, all we have to do is
follow the plan. Here it goes!

29
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:47,690
Now!

30
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,980
I'll remove just the bottle.

31
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:03,097
Then, we'll move in using the
barrier to keep out the flames,

32
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,651
heat, and carbon dioxide.

33
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:15,620
It'll be okay.

34
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:17,625
I can block any kind of magic.

35
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,820
You managed to defend against that?

36
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,120
I see.

37
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,200
That pale blue light must
be a barrier. Uh-huh!

38
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,720
Mm-ya!

39
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:46,770
Mommy!

40
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:51,557
Skeleton V!

41
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,517
Where did these reinforcements come from?

42
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,677
We can't count on the others for help.

43
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,780
You better go.

44
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:59,757
There's something suspicious
about that box on your back.

45
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,960
Beats me.

46
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:03,420
I don't know what you're talking about!

47
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:06,200
Oh, stones are ice! What?

48
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,900
You can withstand this?

49
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,664
Then I'll simply blow you
and that barrier away!

50
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,760
Huh, that was too easy.

51
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,780
What's going on?

52
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:25,620
Is she using magic to withstand the winds?

53
00:03:25,820 --> 00:03:27,761
Nope, it's her blessing of might.

54
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,840
This is nothing!

55
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,355
It'll take more than some bad weather!

56
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:35,580
Forward! Don't stop!

57
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,260
Can't lose!

58
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:41,620
I see now.

59
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:45,078
It seems I've misunderstood
the source of your power.

60
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:50,005
But there's absolutely nothing you can do
before this battle or worth an expense!

61
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:52,020
Honor your baleful wales!

62
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:56,290
Hey!

63
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:57,240
That's no way!

64
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,700
Form change!

65
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:02,340
Thanks, Voxo!

66
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,700
Hello there!

67
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,720
Shores of Earth, close!

68
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,200
Curse, you girl!

69
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:15,340
I got it!

70
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,920
That was great, Shui!

71
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:21,440
That's not enough to stop me! Oh yeah?

72
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:24,173
Why don't you try this on for size then?

73
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:25,510
Voxo?

74
00:04:25,593 --> 00:04:26,423
Yeah!

75
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,530
Oh!

76
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,530
Yeah!

77
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,918
I can't believe it!

78
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:55,560
That was amazing!

79
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:01,880
I gotta say, I didn't expect you to take
down the King of Souls so easily. Duh!

80
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:06,512
If Lamas can get her power under control,
she'd pretty much be unstoppable.

81
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,440
How dare you!

82
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,915
Who the hell do you people think I am?

83
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,660
Enough of that.

84
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,197
Figures an undead
doesn't know when to die.

85
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:19,457
You deserve to suffer a thousand
deaths for treading upon my greatness.

86
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,897
Yeah, that's rich coming
from a talking skeleton.

87
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:24,997
Give me one reason I shouldn't smash
you to bits and collect your coin.

88
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,780
You love my coin?

89
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,440
You think I'm a new stratum lord?

90
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,960
This is really bad! Get away!

91
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,640
Wait, what?

92
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:48,817
How come everything's gone black?

93
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:50,600
Points reduced by 500.

94
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,160
Is it over?

95
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,820
Guys, get up!

96
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:04,520
This is bad.

97
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:17,980
You're the first adventurers to
have survived my dark torrent.

98
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:21,957
I'll take back this arm of
the dead that clings to life.

99
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,700
It doesn't belong to you.

100
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:37,360
Not just anyone deserves to
use such a superior magic item.

101
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:42,260
Wouldn't you agree, old visitor
from another world? Hold up.

102
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:43,680
He knows who I am?

103
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,340
Who are you supposed to be?

104
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:50,377
My name has long been
forgotten by your kind.

105
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:54,220
Though I suppose I've been
referred to as the Netherlord.

106
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:00,000
So, this is the Stratum Lord's coin?

107
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,960
What an amusing bubble.

108
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,482
Why did you attack us like that?

109
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:09,980
Why do you ask?

110
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,640
What other reason does one need to hunt?

111
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,737
Didn't you yourself
come to this stratum to

112
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:18,357
kill the King of Souls
for your own benefit?

113
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,357
It's not the same!

114
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,860
Then please enlighten me.

115
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,022
What makes it somehow different?

116
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,140
Well, human...

117
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,920
How unfortunate.

118
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,900
That was a phantom.

119
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,940
No, Mishuel!

120
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,820
An attack from behind!

121
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,980
We were in the middle of a conversation.

122
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,257
Have you forgotten what matters?

123
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:52,620
Don't try to bite that thing head
on, it's too dangerous! Poxo! On it!

124
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,740
Oh, don't tell me that's all you've got!

125
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:58,920
How about this?

126
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,498
Now's our chance to get out of here!

127
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,630
Oh?

128
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,880
We've gotta go!

129
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,020
Time to leave!

130
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,560
You aren't going anywhere!

131
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,160
You're a troublesome one.

132
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,360
Kill me!

133
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:29,660
Despite everything, you
attack me from behind again!

134
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,020
Shui!

135
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:39,520
Don't touch them, you monster!

136
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:40,980
Lamas, get away!

137
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,180
Please, hurry!

138
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,340
Take the others and run!

139
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:50,000
Oh, what a treat.

140
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:53,740
Getting to see the human
spirit of self-sacrifice.

141
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:55,280
Very well.

142
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:01,420
Stop it!

143
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,952
Let you give me a treat!

144
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:15,020
You can't be gone.

145
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:19,142
You promised you'd always be there
to help me out, no matter what.

146
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:21,927
Everyone at the orphanage
is counting on you.

147
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:24,720
Get up. Please.

148
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,437
I'm begging you, open your eyes!

149
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,660
You can't be dead!

150
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,537
Cry all you want.

151
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:33,820
But they won't be waking up again.

152
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,250
Oh, no.

153
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:43,866
Llamas is totally out
of control at this rate.

154
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:51,020
You hurt too bad.

155
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:53,200
I know that, Boxxo.

156
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,557
There's no way I can hit him like this.

157
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,260
Hello there. But still,

158
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:01,932
if we can't figure out some way to stop
him, Everybody's going to die here!

159
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:02,930
You're right!

160
00:10:03,013 --> 00:10:04,837
That's why I came up with a plan!

161
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:09,449
But if it doesn't work out, you could
potentially lose your life for nothing!

162
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:11,820
What's the matter?

163
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,700
Have you already given up?

164
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:19,440
I was hoping you would provide me with
a bit more entertainment, you bore!

165
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,680
Please block it!

166
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,340
How dreadfully prosaic.

167
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,120
Thanks for that, Boxo.

168
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:31,560
Hello there.

169
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:36,397
I know you'll come up with
a way to beat this creep.

170
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,680
And until then, I won't ever give up.

171
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:40,890
That's right.

172
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,295
She's counting on me.

173
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,658
I have to put my trust into her too.

174
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,220
Huh? Boxo?

175
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,027
You could even win a reward.

176
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,500
Oh, I see.

177
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,857
Have you already thought of a plan?

178
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,480
Hello there. Great!

179
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,280
Let's do this, then.

180
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:04,780
It appears you've finished saying
your final goodbyes to each other.

181
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,660
Fear not, I am not a cruel being.

182
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:12,160
I will reunite you with your
dearly-deported friends soon enough,

183
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:15,580
using my most powerful
technique! It's time!

184
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:19,899
For the first step, I'll use my
barrier to eject Lamas at full power!

185
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,480
Here we go! No!

186
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,400
Now for step two.

187
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,247
I'll shoot the balloons out.

188
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:31,970
Absurd.

189
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:53,440
To think you were able to
shatter the arm of the dead.

190
00:11:56,840 --> 00:12:00,477
I look forward to seeing how
your group develops further.

191
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:03,720
I'll be waiting for you
to come and find me.

192
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:11,520
Yulemi, wake up!

193
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,280
You promised you'd help me.

194
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:19,817
You can't make good on your promise if
you die and leave me all alone, right?

195
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,680
Please, open your eyes.

196
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:26,240
Yulemi, Shui, there's still
so much we have to do.

197
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:27,754
This can't be the end.

198
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:31,736
That son of a bitch!

199
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,500
Shui! Shui!

200
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,980
I won't let you go!

201
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,197
Nobody in the Menagerie of
Bulls is allowed to die!

202
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:42,397
What do we do, Captain?

203
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,617
Don't just sit there!

204
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:47,137
Didn't the association teach you
what to do in these situations?

205
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,050
Right.

206
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:50,609
Is that a cardiac massage?

207
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,567
Hold on, I think I've
got something for this.

208
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:54,550
I do!

209
00:12:58,660 --> 00:12:59,490
Huh?

210
00:12:59,573 --> 00:13:01,597
For Boxer to change forms all of a sudden,

211
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,677
that must mean he's got
an item up his sleeve.

212
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,437
I agree, but I've never
seen this form before.

213
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,579
Yeah, that tracks.

214
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:12,037
Even in my old world, the average person
probably wouldn't know how to use an AED.

215
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,897
How can I expect the people of
this world to understand it?

216
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,921
But I don't have time to explain!

217
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:21,513
I don't care how many points this costs!

218
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:26,280
Huh? It's floating!

219
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,357
Are you saying this'll save them?

220
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,280
Hello there!

221
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:35,897
Expose the patient's chest and retrieve
the square bag from underneath the lid.

222
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,960
Afterwards, tear open the
bag and remove the pads.

223
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:40,400
Sure, on it!

224
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,420
Now for the hard part.

225
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:45,357
In order to maximize the
chance that this'll work,

226
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:48,616
I'll increase my dexterity
with the rest of my points!

227
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:52,080
I'm finished, Boxo! Is this good?

228
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:54,620
Hello there. Right.

229
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:55,860
First off...

230
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:03,200
Please do not touch the patient.

231
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,220
Now recording EKG.

232
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,740
Scan complete. Reading measurements.

233
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:09,897
Electric shock is required.

234
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:11,357
Move away from the body.

235
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,100
This has to work!

236
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,680
Electric shock has been performed.

237
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,572
Begin manual cardiac massage immediately.

238
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:21,810
Okay.

239
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:27,950
Oh no.

240
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,320
I was too late.

241
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:31,896
If only I had thought of this sooner.

242
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,720
Yulami, why aren't you waking up?

243
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:37,697
Voxo gave us a special item
to help bring you back.

244
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:40,320
So please open your eyes. Yulami!

245
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:46,930
Lamas?

246
00:14:47,013 --> 00:14:47,860
What happened?

247
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:49,930
Yulami!

248
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,520
Voxo, come on, Jusui!

249
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,640
Hello there!

250
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:58,950
Captain?

251
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:01,820
What's going on?

252
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:02,980
Did we win?

253
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:06,498
Don't need to be careful, you dummy!

254
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:08,930
Hold on!

255
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:10,957
That's so hard, I can't breathe!

256
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,864
Thank goodness they're alright!

257
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:16,121
Seems the people here are
sturdier than I thought.

258
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:20,917
I'm sorry for being so
useless during the fight.

259
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:25,257
You put your trust in me, and when it
really counted, I wasn't able to save you.

260
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,337
No need to apologize.

261
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:30,177
I talked a big game, but in the end,
I wasn't able to do anything either.

262
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:31,120
Yes, I'm here.

263
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:33,580
That was the Netherlord, huh?

264
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,280
He's seriously bad news.

265
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:39,396
We have to let Director Bear
know as soon as possible.

266
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,417
He was truly a monstrous opponent.

267
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:46,971
If we were to fight him again, I'm not
sure I'd be able to protect everyone.

268
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,220
Several days later,

269
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,557
after Hulemy and Shui had fully recovered,

270
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,640
we made our way back to
the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

271
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,340
As soon as we arrived,

272
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:59,857
the first thing we did was report
the incident to Director Bear.

273
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:00,780
I see.

274
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:02,937
And you're sure he was the Netherlord?

275
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:04,537
Sounds like you've heard of him before.

276
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:05,450
Indeed.

277
00:16:05,533 --> 00:16:07,277
Though I don't know much
since I've only read his

278
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:10,177
name in passing while
perusing some old records.

279
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:13,319
But I suspect he's a general
serving the Demon Lord.

280
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:14,770
Hold on.

281
00:16:14,853 --> 00:16:17,257
You're saying there's someone
even stronger than him?

282
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,217
In light of this new information,

283
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:22,997
I'll be requesting an emergency meeting
with the directors of each stratum.

284
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,080
You've done well.

285
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:27,717
I want you to get plenty of rest in
case anything unexpected happens.

286
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,630
Right.

287
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:33,280
Hey, missus! I'm back!

288
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,760
Oh, Lamas!

289
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:35,940
I was worried.

290
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:37,817
Please tell me you're all right.

291
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:38,730
Yep.

292
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,940
You're finally back!

293
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:45,100
Oh. Huh.

294
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,917
Why do I feel like I've
seen this scene before?

295
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:48,830
Are you okay?

296
00:16:48,913 --> 00:16:50,417
You're not hurt anywhere, are you?

297
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:51,330
Calm down.

298
00:16:51,413 --> 00:16:52,260
I'm fine.

299
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:53,762
Thank goodness.

300
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,277
I heard you ran into an enemy that
was stronger than a stratum lord,

301
00:16:57,360 --> 00:17:00,301
and I was so worried I
couldn't even sleep a wink.

302
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:02,640
Don't worry, Munami. I'm home.

303
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:05,690
Apparently,

304
00:17:05,773 --> 00:17:08,077
the story about us fighting
the nether lord had already

305
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,377
started spreading throughout
the village like wildfire.

306
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,997
We heard about what happened, Boxo.

307
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:15,157
It's a good thing you were there,
otherwise things could have been bad.

308
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,070
Too bad.

309
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,416
Don't be modest now.

310
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:19,997
You drove off a monster
stronger than a stratum

311
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,937
lord and saved Hulemy and
Shui while you were at it.

312
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:24,477
After everything you've done for us,

313
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:28,377
it's safe to say you're an irreplaceable
part of this village, Boxo.

314
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:31,048
It's really nice to
hear that kind of stuff.

315
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:32,517
But still...

316
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:36,500
Tale of your heroism has
spread far and wide, Mr. Boxo.

317
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:41,315
Hearing of it has only strengthened
my desire to bring you into my home.

318
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:43,917
Unfortunately, until that day comes,

319
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,059
you'll just have to put up
with living with Mommies!

320
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,190
Huh?

321
00:17:49,273 --> 00:17:51,040
What was that about? Who knows?

322
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:56,527
Why are there so many
people in this village?

323
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,480
Mr. Mishel!

324
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,497
Yes! Who is...

325
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,857
Oh, it's you guys.

326
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:04,637
Did you need something from me?

327
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:07,877
We were wondering if you had
any other plans after this.

328
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:08,790
What?

329
00:18:08,873 --> 00:18:10,477
We're going after the Nether Lord.

330
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:13,037
But to be honest, he's
so strong, it's scary.

331
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,857
Please keep fighting by our sides.

332
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:16,528
We can't do it without you.

333
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:20,420
I don't know how much use I'd be.

334
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:24,940
He defeated me handily.
Mr. Mishel? That's why.

335
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:27,180
I swear upon my blade.

336
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,420
Next time, I won't lose.

337
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:34,605
I promise from this day forth, I won't
allow any of my comrades to be hurt again.

338
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,750
Hooray!

339
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:41,860
By the way,

340
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,637
Director Bear said he was going to summon

341
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:46,367
expert hunters from each
of the other strata.

342
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:48,400
Like 40 or 50 people, right?

343
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,937
More than that, I heard him throw
around numbers in the hundreds.

344
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:55,608
If we really push, we could
probably recruit over a thousand.

345
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:58,577
There's no way we could lose, right, Mr.

346
00:18:58,660 --> 00:18:59,490
Mishel?

347
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,200
But of course.

348
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:10,957
What's on your mind, Captain?

349
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,140
Are you okay?

350
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:16,037
I'm trying to figure out exactly what
we're hoping to achieve out here.

351
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:16,950
What?

352
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:20,637
I've always thought that as long as
I'm working towards getting my wish,

353
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,426
it'd be all right if I
dropped dead somewhere.

354
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:24,430
But now,

355
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:25,880
I've been thinking,

356
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:30,677
what gives me the right to put the lives
of my people at risk to achieve some goal,

357
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,878
one that might not even be possible?

358
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,600
It's not like that.

359
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:39,640
I never would have imagined hearing
such spineless words out of you.

360
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:40,610
That's right.

361
00:19:40,693 --> 00:19:43,442
Also, that serious look
doesn't match you at all.

362
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:44,670
You guys.

363
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:48,777
We knew the risks when we joined
up with the Menagerie of Fools.

364
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:51,557
Don't think for even a second
that you have to coddle us.

365
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,470
See, Captain?

366
00:19:52,620 --> 00:19:54,657
All you have to do is keep moving forward.

367
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:56,077
You can leave the rear to us.

368
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:58,617
We believe in you, so
keep your head up, okay?

369
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,797
They're right, you know.

370
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:02,115
I couldn't have said it better myself.

371
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:08,034
I get it already, so enough
with all the sappy speeches.

372
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,097
All right, then.

373
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:10,757
We're heading out tomorrow.

374
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:13,957
Akka, Shiro, gather up rations
and supplies for 30 days.

375
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,397
She'll be getting a tab, too.

376
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,310
Huh?

377
00:20:16,393 --> 00:20:17,297
What do you mean, 30 days?

378
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:18,800
And you want us to pay?

379
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:23,353
Speaking of, Captain, I believe you
still owe us our wages for this month.

380
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:27,700
One morning,

381
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:31,777
Lamas put me on her back and left the
village without saying where we were going.

382
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:33,460
We walked along in silence.

383
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:35,810
Hmm.

384
00:20:35,893 --> 00:20:37,440
I wonder where she's taking me.

385
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,720
Here we are, Boxo.

386
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:44,700
Hold on.

387
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:47,000
Do you recognize this place?

388
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:50,456
This is the exact spot you
and I first met each other.

389
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:51,720
Hello there!

390
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,560
Also, this is where you first saved me.

391
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,980
I still remember it.

392
00:20:58,220 --> 00:20:59,050
Lamas...

393
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:02,797
So many things have happened
since I got to know you.

394
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,400
Lots of it was dangerous.

395
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:06,170
are scary.

396
00:21:06,253 --> 00:21:08,457
But no matter what
happened on our adventures,

397
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:11,952
you always helped out and you
made sure everyone was safe.

398
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:14,060
You're wrong, Lamas.

399
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:16,357
We've just been lucky up to this point.

400
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:19,720
Our last battle made that
painfully obvious. Voxo,

401
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,637
something tells me that
you're blaming yourself

402
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:24,485
for what happened in the
Dead's Lament stratum.

403
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:27,517
But that's not true.

404
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,040
It's not your fault.

405
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:33,257
In fact, the only reason I was
unharmed was because you were there.

406
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:34,337
If it weren't for you,

407
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:37,657
we wouldn't have been able to save
Hulemy and Shui and they would have died.

408
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:38,880
So that's why.

409
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:41,691
You shouldn't feel down on yourself, okay?

410
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,820
You did nothing wrong.

411
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,550
Lamas,

412
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:53,181
it's amazing how much empathy you can show
towards a simple vending machine like me.

413
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:57,277
Huh, and here we were thinking
you might need some cheering up.

414
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,237
Looks like Lamas already has it covered.

415
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,150
Huh?

416
00:22:00,233 --> 00:22:02,780
Yolami, Shui, how'd you find us?

417
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:04,160
How do you think?

418
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:08,417
We followed you after we heard you left
the village with Boxxo on your back.

419
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:09,340
Oh, dang.

420
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:13,720
And besides, we still haven't
thanked him for saving us.

421
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:14,999
Yep, that's right.

422
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:17,100
Wait, hold on a sec.

423
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:20,540
Back off!

424
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:23,037
I mean, what the heck are
you two doing to Boxxo?

425
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:25,237
We're just showing him our gratitude.

426
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,837
After all, if it weren't for
him, we'd be in the afterlife.

427
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:31,214
Come to think of it, you owe
Boxo a lot, too, don't you?

428
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:33,797
You could thank him
now and then, you know.

429
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:34,821
Well, thank him?

430
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:38,817
I guess it's only fair if
I give him a reward, too.

431
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:42,277
Plus, Mom would always remind me
it's polite to give proper thanks.

432
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,300
It's happening.

433
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:50,960
I can't do it, Boxo.

434
00:22:51,060 --> 00:22:51,980
I'm so sorry.

435
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,797
I'm about to die from
embarrassment, Olive.

436
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,500
It's stalling. Just go.

437
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,070
Hey!

438
00:23:11,220 --> 00:23:12,540
You jerks!

439
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:16,100
You finally did it!

440
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,860
You came for this! Come here!

441
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:24,357
Being reborn as a vending
machine to wander the

442
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:27,360
dungeon in another world
is a ridiculous premise.

443
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:31,197
But after everything I've been through
and meeting a bunch of new people,

444
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:34,097
I think I'd like to keep
living this kind of life.
